    description: "The `directness` meta key (values: direct / transitive / undeclared) is WRITE-ONLY. Tier-axis concept audit (2026-07-15): stamped at ir.py:1504 (create_boundary_nodes, gated to go/java/kotlin/python + a non-None DependencyManifest), classified by DependencyManifest.classify_directness (supply_chain.py:107), and registered as a MetaKeySpec axis (axis_meta_keys.py:469) — but has ZERO readers (grep for .get(\"directness\") / meta[\"directness\"] read = 0). ADR-0041 §2 extracted directness FROM tier so \"the direct/transitive knowledge the classifier was burning into the tier is re-emitted as the directness stamp\" — the extraction correctly purified tier, but nothing consumes the re-emitted stamp. (Contrast: `ecosystem`, the ADR-0041 §3 extraction, has one report-only reader at cli.py:8562.)\n\nOPTIONS: (a) wire a consumer — surface directness in explain / supply_chain_summary; (b) mark it an explicit x-internal extension point in the schema (like AnalysisRun.run_signature, kept for external PROV-DM tooling); (c) remove the stamp + classifier if genuinely unwanted. Parallels the provenance-audit dead field origin_run_signature (WI-gapin). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-supply_chain_tier_07152026.md (F4)."  # 14e9
